challenges in ML

1: data collection

2: insufficient data / labeled Data
  --> whey you have more data you can train better

3: non representative data
  --> sampling noise
  --> sampling bias
  e.g: you have to ask each and every one about the cricket match 
  and get the result from that 


4: Poor Quality Data
--> garbage in garbage out 
    (if you put bad quality data then you will get bad quality output)

5: irrelevent features

6: overfitting

7: underfitting

8: software integration
if you want to put ml model in arduino , then that is problem 

9: offline deployment : online learning is costly 

